  "description": {
   "value": "<p><strong>Cost:</strong> 1,000eb (Very Expensive)<br>\n<strong>Enhances:</strong> Monowire<br>\n<strong>Option Slots:</strong> 0 (Cyberware Enhancement)</p>\n<p>Enhances a Monowire and sits outside its enhancement limit. Spend an Action and 4 hours to write a Quickhack of Standard Difficulty (DV8) or easier into the wire, or to trade out whichever one is already there; while it lives in the wire it is unavailable for ordinary netrunning. With Combat Software (Data Tunnelling) installed, the user may trade away their Move Action once per combat to charge this, and the Action after that has to be a ROF 1 attack through it or the charge bleeds off. Landing that attack adds 1d6 damage (3d6), counts as a direct Jack In to the victim's Neuroport, and hands a Netrunner a free Net Action for that Turn alone, restricted to the Quickhack in the wire.</p>\n<p><strong>Foundry notes:</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li>Corgo's required content includes the Edgerunners Mission Kit and Interface RED, and this parent piece comes from there rather than from Cyberpunk RED - Core, which ships no item for it. Make the parent yourself before installing this into it.</li>\n</ul>\n<p><em>From <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/13EnSAoiLDsC7zmL-Jr1RqIh_EnuVuFnExqiipDVquMk/edit\">Corgo's 77 Collection V3</a> by Corgopolis (Cyberware &gt; Cyberarms).</em></p>"
